  "findings": [
    "Ballistic beams, common absorption, local epsilon derivative and periodic wavenumber fix a unique signed energy-density output without a solver mandate. Neutral replacement permission is byte-identical.",
    "M1 tensor derivative is correct: energy derivative at fixed flux and flux-direction derivatives retained. At zero flux only dP_xx/dE=1/3 survives. Common absorption leaves the background flux factor constant, so the matrix exponential exactly solves this closure.",
    "Beam characteristic translation independently yields the full angular transport solution. Copropagating and uniform anchors preserve the intended calibration degeneracy.",
    "Fixed sigma is independent of the unknown parameter. Public image contains only README/model/public tests/data; true parameter, hints, reference and hidden groups remain private.",
    "Existing validator demonstrates 256 oracle passes and shortcut rejections, derivative agreement 2.3e-10, real-space second-order convergence, local oracle9/9 and shortcut6pass/3intended failures. No claim about empirical agent difficulty."
